In A-NAS the page is the card's host: there is no dsh-pet HTTP host behind ROUTE_PATH. The card
sends three actions to its host with postAction, the playback receipts (playback-report.ts),
waking the pet when it is clicked asleep and releasing the lock when it is grabbed (runtime.ts);
setActionHandler lets the page answer them in place, at the same routes and with the same
bodies, so neither caller changes. Without a handler they go to the network as before.

